    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "those ideas are great. i also want to tackle the idea that current regulations (like age verification or content moderation laws) are being used as a way to socially engineer what people are \"allowed\" to see. how would a philosopher like Mill or even a modern libertarian argue that this kind of \"protection\" is actually just state-sponsored censorship?",
